    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133-a1">

                <pb facs="0357" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v32/pg322"/>

                <head>Attachment<anchor n="7" xml:id="d133-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">CRITERIA</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Degree</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>A.</label>
                    <item>Membership in either the Movimiento Popular Dominicano (MPD), the Partido Comunista Dominicano (PCD), or the Agrupacion Politica Catorce del
                        Julio (APCJ) [current membership in
                            latter]<anchor n="8" xml:id="d133-f2"/> will serve as a bar to
                        governmental employment in all levels of the government.</item>
                    <pb facs="0358" n="323" xml:id="pg323"/>
                    <label>B.</label>
                    <item>A significant range of Communist affiliation and association (including
                        family ties) but no known membership will serve as a bar at all levels of
                        sensitive ministries, i.e., Defense, Interior, Justice, Propaganda,
                        Education, and the Judiciary, but may be permitted in limited quantity in
                        non-sensitive ministries.</item>
                    <label>C.</label>
                    <item>Where there are some reports of limited reliability of Communist
                        associations and/or attachments balanced on whole or in part by favorable
                        reporting, individuals would be barred only from the top echelon of
                        sensitive ministries.</item>
                </list>
                <p>It should be clearly understood that as we get government employees beyond the
                    second level in ministries, there will be less likelihood that our files will
                    contain traces.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
